## Why This Is Asked
This checks practical ability to implement stable background work with WorkManager, persistent config storage via DataStore, and a simple UI-facing trigger.

## Key Concepts
- WorkManager periodic tasks with constraints
- CoroutineWorker pattern
- DataStore for small config persistence
- Flow/LiveData for UI updates
- Retry/backoff and error handling

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Serializable
data class Config(val version: String, val features: Map<String, Boolean>)

class ConfigWorker(appContext: Context, params: WorkerParameters) : CoroutineWorker(appContext, params) {
    override suspend fun doWork(): Result {
        val url = inputData.getString("url") ?: return Result.failure()
        // network fetch and parse omitted for brevity
        return Result.success()
    }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test failure scenarios (network error, invalid JSON)?
- How would you prevent duplicate work when the app restarts?

## Why This Is Asked

New angle introduces multi-cache offline view and scheduled refresh, probing data modeling, cache invalidation, and basic MVVM patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Room entities and relations
- Separate body cache design
- MVVM with Repository
- WorkManager with constraints
- Simple search SQL LIKE

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "article_meta")
data class ArticleMeta(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val excerpt: String,
  val updatedAt: Long
)

@Entity(tableName = "article_body")
data class ArticleBody(
  @PrimaryKey val articleId: String,
  val body: String
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM article_meta WHERE title LIKE :query || '%'")
  fun searchByTitle(query: String): List<ArticleMeta>

  @Transaction
  @Query("SELECT * FROM article_meta WHERE id = :id")
  fun getArticleWithBody(id: String): ArticleWithBody
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle cache invalidation and staleness if the remote API updates articles?
- What tests would you write to verify offline viewing, search correctness, and refresh reliability?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model data, persist with Room, export data offline, and share via intents. Emphasizes file access patterns and compatibility.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, and a simple Repository
- JSON serialization of data
- FileProvider and content URIs
- Sharing via ACTION_SEND
- Runtime permissions considerations on older Android versions

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "notes")
data class Note(
  @PrimaryKey val id: Int,
  val title: String,
  val content: String,
  val createdAt: Long
)

@Dao interface NoteDao { @Query("SELECT * FROM notes ORDER BY createdAt DESC") fun getAllNotes(): List<Note> }

class NoteRepository(private val context: Context, private val dao: NoteDao) {
  fun exportNotes(): Uri {
    val notes = dao.getAllNotes()
    val json = Gson().toJson(notes)
    val dir = context.getExternalFilesDir(null)!!
    val file = File(dir, "notes.json")
    file.writeText(json)
    return FileProvider.getUriForFile(context, "com.example.fileprovider", file)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle large note datasets to avoid O(n) memory usage during export?
- How would you test FileProvider permissions and share intent across Android versions?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical Compose performance debugging, not just theory.

## Key Concepts

- Compose recomposition profiling
- Stable keys in LazyColumn
- Extracting item composables
- Immutable data models with stable ids
- Derived state and remember patterns
- SnapshotFlow and diffing for list updates

## Code Example

```kotlin
data class Article(val id: String, val title: String, val body: String)

@Composable
fun ArticleRow(article: Article) {
  Text(text = article.title)
}

@Composable
fun NewsFeed(articles: List<Article>) {
  LazyColumn { 
    items(articles, key = { it.id }) { article ->
      ArticleRow(article)
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure the impact of introducing a DiffUtil-like mechanism for the list?
- What edge cases could cause misleading recomposition counts and how would you guard against them?

